  "worked_solution": "Let's refer to our standard ${30}^{∘}$-${60}^{∘}$-${90}^{∘}$ triangle. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14165760/assets/032bc058139e8f2b9381510a1f5817b73632b1015f3bc0a364e227001c383bb8.png)\n\nSince the hypotenuse has a length of $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =2 \\\\ x & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now calculate the length of the longer leg as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3}x=\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 1=\\sqrt{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the longer leg has a length of $\\sqrt{3}.$",
